{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Getting a Meal "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for Help and Advice "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this. <br/><br/>Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help. This is called a question within a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Can/Could + you + verb</span> (show/tell/explain) + (to) me <span class=\"strong\">+ question word</span> (how ... why ... where ... who ... etc.)<br/>Notice how most of these examples end with a verb.  If the question word is \u201chow to\u201d, there is no verb at the end."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can/Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Question Word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">what</span> some problems are?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explain to me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">how</span> a restaurant works?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">where</span> the washroom is?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you tell me what some problems are?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you explain to me how a restaurant works?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you show me how to organize a work schedule?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Discussing How to Deal with Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "One way to discuss how to deal with problems is to say what you would do if you were in someone else's situation. This is a polite way of communicating if you use the modals <span class =\"italic\">would</span> or <span class =\"italic\">could</span>.<span class=\"italic\"><br/><br/>I would ... <br/>I wouldn't ... <br/>You could ... </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are examples of Peter giving Vanessa suggestions about how to deal with the problems she is discussing."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It is difficult to keep track of fresh food. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I would make a list of ingredients and then do an inventory."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Another problem is making sure we have the right number of staff members to serve the clientele. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I wouldn't want people to come to work on a slow night. You could have some employees on backup."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "clientele"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the people who purchase goods or services, like meals at a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Another problem is making sure we have the right number of staff members to serve the clientele. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob02aud01"}], "type": 